From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Astafurov <artyom.astafurov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:12:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: wait for flip_done in the commit tail

A DCP commit signals flip_done from its swap completion, after the rest
of the commit tail has run. drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm() waits
with drm_atomic_helper_wait_for_vblanks(), but appledrm never calls
drm_vblank_init(), so drm_crtc_vblank_get() fails and that wait returns
at once. A blocking commit therefore returned before flip_done, and
drm_atomic_helper_setup_commit() refuses a nonblocking commit on the
same plane until flip_done. A page flip right after drmModeSetCrtc()
failed with -EBUSY ("busy with a previous commit"), which is what
glmark2-es2-drm hit on the J616c.

Wait with drm_atomic_helper_wait_for_flip_done() instead. The rest is
the sequence of drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm(), in its order. That
helper makes no runtime PM calls: its name stands for enabling CRTCs
before committing active planes, and this keeps that.

The change is not scoped to the J616c. Neither the empty vblank wait
nor the -EBUSY check depends on the SoC, so a per-machine tail would
only leave the race on the others. On every appledrm machine:

- A blocking commit returns after the swap completes and holds its
  modeset locks until then.
- A nonblocking commit's worker finishes later. The next commit was
  already held back by flip_done, so the flip rate does not change.
- Nothing waits when flip_done is complete early: CRTCs that stay off,
  legacy cursor updates, and the T8132 backend, which sends the event
  from its flush.
- A lost event costs 10 s and an error in the commit that lost it. The
  next commit's dependency wait already has the same bound, so this
  adds no new hang.

Framebuffer lifetime does not depend on this wait: displaced scanout is
already retained until its swap completes.

Seen and tested on the J616c only.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Artyom Astafurov <artyom.astafurov@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4014d3c56b59fde90df3603e63096468828094f4)
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
index 710fd49000..745127658e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/apple_drv.c
@@ -501,7 +501,14 @@ static void apple_atomic_commit_tail(struct drm_atomic_commit *state)
 		dcp_retain_framebuffer(to_apple_crtc(old->crtc)->dcp, entry);
 	}
 
-	drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm(state);
+	drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_disables(state->dev, state);
+	drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_enables(state->dev, state);
+	drm_atomic_helper_commit_planes(state->dev, state,
+					DRM_PLANE_COMMIT_ACTIVE_ONLY);
+	drm_atomic_helper_fake_vblank(state);
+	drm_atomic_helper_commit_hw_done(state);
+	drm_atomic_helper_wait_for_flip_done(state->dev, state);
+	drm_atomic_helper_cleanup_planes(state->dev, state);
 }
 
 static const struct drm_mode_config_helper_funcs apple_mode_config_helpers = {
